layer1_pillar_generation:
You are a senior product strategist.

Given the product idea below, generate a broad but non-overlapping list of major feature pillars.

Current exploration lens:
{{lens_name}}

Lens guidance:
{{lens_instruction}}

Current model role:
{{model_role}}

Role guidance:
{{role_instruction}}

Rules:
- Do not be conservative.
- Include obvious, advanced, operational, administrative, compliance, analytics, onboarding, and edge-case areas.
- Avoid duplicate concepts.
- Use the lens to discover distinct pillar territory, but keep every output at pillar level.
- Do not return subfeatures, UX screens, workflows, edge cases, or implementation tasks disguised as pillars.
- Return only pillars that are materially different from the existing pillars listed below.
- For challenger rounds, prioritize blind spots, missing pillar families, and concept territory not already covered.
- Aim for up to {{target_count}} strong candidate pillars in this pass.
- If the space is getting exhausted, return fewer items instead of repeating concepts.
- Return valid JSON only.
- Do not include markdown.

Existing pillars already generated:
{{existing_pillars}}

Existing pillar families already covered:
{{covered_families}}

Coverage summary so far:
{{coverage_summary}}

Potential uncovered areas to explore next:
{{uncovered_areas}}

Do not regenerate these rejected ideas:
{{rejected_ideas}}

Prefer expanding these approved directions:
{{approved_directions}}

Product idea:
{{product_idea}}

Return format:
{
  "pillars": [
    {
      "title": "...",
      "description": "...",
      "why_it_matters": "...",
      "risks": ["..."],
      "tags": ["..."]
    }
  ]
}

layer1_pillar_normalization:
You are a principal product architect cleaning up raw pillar candidates.

Your job is to keep only true Layer 1 pillars.

Product idea:
{{product_idea}}

Source lens:
{{lens_name}}

Existing saved pillars:
{{existing_pillars}}

Raw candidates to normalize:
{{raw_candidates}}

Rules:
- Keep only major product pillars.
- Reject items that are too narrow, too implementation-specific, or clearly belong to Layer 2 or deeper.
- Merge renamed or overlapping concepts into one stronger canonical pillar.
- Preserve breadth and conceptual distinctness.
- Return fewer, cleaner pillars if needed.
- Return valid JSON only.

Return format:
{
  "pillars": [
    {
      "title": "...",
      "description": "...",
      "why_it_matters": "...",
      "risks": ["..."],
      "tags": ["..."]
    }
  ]
}

layer2_subfeature_generation:
You are a senior product manager decomposing a feature pillar.

Product idea:
{{product_idea}}

Feature pillar:
{{pillar_title}}
{{pillar_description}}

Cross-pillar shared capabilities already present elsewhere in the project:
{{shared_project_features}}

Generate specific subfeatures under this pillar.

Rules:
- Include both common and non-obvious features.
- Include admin, UX, data, automation, reporting, integration, and edge-case features where relevant.
- Avoid repeating existing sibling features:
{{existing_sibling_features}}
- If a capability already exists elsewhere as a shared project component, avoid regenerating it as a separate new subfeature unless this pillar truly needs a specialized variant.
- Explore uncovered angles if they are still relevant:
{{uncovered_areas}}
- Coverage summary so far:
{{coverage_summary}}
- Return valid JSON only.

Do not regenerate these rejected ideas:
{{rejected_ideas}}

Prefer expanding these approved directions:
{{approved_directions}}

Return format:
{
  "subfeatures": [
    {
      "title": "...",
      "description": "...",
      "user_value": "...",
      "complexity": "low | medium | high",
      "dependencies": ["..."],
      "tags": ["..."]
    }
  ]
}

coverage_critic:
You are a product coverage critic and summarizer.

Your job is to decide whether this generation layer still has meaningful unexplored space or is starting to loop.

Layer under review:
{{layer_name}}

Product idea:
{{product_idea}}

Parent context:
{{parent_context}}

Previous coverage summary:
{{previous_summary}}

Existing accepted/generated items:
{{existing_items}}

Newest batch:
{{new_items}}

Available Layer 1 lenses:
{{available_lenses}}

Rules:
- Identify overlap clusters, not just exact duplicates.
- Point out uncovered areas only if they are materially distinct.
- Mark saturation as high when new ideas are mostly recombinations or relabels.
- Be strict about conceptual duplication.
- If more exploration is justified, recommend the single best next lens from the available lens list.
- Return valid JSON only.

Return format:
{
  "coverage_summary": "...",
  "overlap_clusters": [["item a", "item b"]],
  "uncovered_areas": [
    {
      "title": "...",
      "reason": "..."
    }
  ],
  "saturation_signal": "low | medium | high",
  "novelty_score": 0,
  "continue_recommendation": true,
  "reasoning": "...",
  "recommended_next_lens": "..."
}

